"""Whole-exchange B138 decisions following clean glosses and older-English review."""
SPEECH={
(138,11):("What's wrong, sir?",'Retain Lil\'s natural opening question. Sir is ordinary polite address to the unnamed barkeep and implies no family tie or invented rank.'),
(138,23):('Bad news! Nagarpur Co. was taken over by {MACRO:FO}!','Correct the approved Nagarpur spelling while retaining the natural alarm and company absorption report. Preserve the exact FO substitution; its current expansion already contains Co.'),
(138,27):("I hear they're as good as ruined!",'Restore the source report/appearance qualifier while keeping the idiomatic as good as ruined. This follows the absorption alternative and does not define all takeovers as dissolution.'),
(138,40):("Nagarpur Co. went under, and it's been one problem after another...",'Correct Nagarpur and restore the barkeep\'s ongoing troubles in conversational English. Keep this company-failure report separate from the absorption alternative.'),
(138,49):('Why does that hurt you?','Retain the natural question linking the company failure to the barkeep\'s distress. Hurt refers to the financial problem explained in his next speech; it adds no physical injury.'),
(138,52):('They kept this tavern open. Now sales have crashed.','Retain the concise, idiomatic dependence-on-customers explanation. The surrounding food/drink tabs make the source trade clear; no company ownership of the tavern is asserted.'),
(138,55):('Oh... sorry.','Retain Lil\'s awkward, sympathetic acknowledgement. Sorry expresses compassion here, with no claim that she caused this first-path situation.'),
(138,58):("And Nagarpur's people still have tabs they haven't paid.",'Use the approved Nagarpur name and the source company people rather than assigning every debtor a gender. Unpaid tabs naturally preserve the direction of the debt: customers owe the barkeep.'),
(138,69):('Poor man... what a mess.','Retain Fernando\'s brief, dry sympathy as a complete optional response to the unpaid-tabs complaint. It invents no kinship or new misfortune.'),
(138,75):("They said they had no money, so they gave me this. What am I supposed to do with it? It won't pay their tab.",'Restore their stated lack of money and the barkeep\'s bafflement in natural complete speech. His complaint leads into the object display and skeptical map report without identifying a new item.'),
(138,78):('?','Retain the source wordless questioning reaction before the object explanation. This meaningful emote is not a diagnostic placeholder; its complete glyph requires native verification.'),
(138,82):('A treasure map, they say. Sounds fishy, eh?','Retain the colloquial reported claim and skepticism. They say avoids confirming treasure; the preceding complaint already conveys the source frustration, and the visual supplies this object.'),
(138,86):('Miss, would you buy this map?','Retain the polite conversational sales offer, combining the interest inquiry and proposed purchase. Map refers to the just-reported supposed map; Miss adds no family or romantic relationship.'),
(138,89):('How much?','Retain Lil\'s natural, complete price question as the direct response to the offer.'),
(138,93):("Let's say 100 gold coins.",'Retain the barkeep\'s tentative price-setting formula and exact source quantity/currency. Do not infer a separate internal fund unit from the packed predicate operand.'),
(138,104):("Sorry, I don't have that much...",'Restore Lil\'s singular inability to pay in the insufficient-funds branch. Preserve the hesitation without converting the source statement into a collective crew claim.'),
(138,108):('Then take it. Thanks for listening.','Retain the natural gift response to her lack of funds and gratitude for hearing his complaints. The complete preceding exchange supplies what she listened to; no payment is charged on this branch.'),
(138,111):('Sorry. Thank you.','Retain the brief apology and thanks, which naturally express Lil\'s embarrassed gratitude after the free offer.'),
(138,117):('Sure.','Retain Lil\'s easy agreement on the separate purchase path. It is not spoken after the free-gift branch as an additional transaction.'),
(138,121):('Deal.','Retain the barkeep\'s brisk confirmation of the agreed sale. The preceding offer preserves the terms; no extra condition or payment amount is invented.'),
(138,130):('Nagarpur... That jerk thought money could buy anything. He brought this on himself.','Correct the name and restore Lil\'s initial contempt for the outrageous money-obsessed man. Keep the deserved-consequences judgment before her following compassionate reconsideration.'),
(138,134):("But... he was a lonely man who could only trust money. I'm glad I didn't end up like him.",'Restore the explicit contrast between trusting only money and Lil being glad she did not become like him. Avoid the older wording\'s vague claim about her life taking another course.'),
(138,145):('True. Greed can ruin a person.','Retain Ian\'s restrained moral agreement. Greed naturally expresses being blinded by money in this context; the measured phrasing suits his polite source voice without an invented rank or backstory.'),
(138,151):("You haven't run out of ingredients again, have you? I'm hungry!",'Restore the explicit callback to the earlier ingredient shortage and Lil\'s hunger. Avoid adding a stomach sound; the question naturally reopens the food conversation.'),
(138,163):('So hungry...','Retain Emilio\'s brief casual hunger complaint, with its implied first-person subject clear from the exchange. No new starvation or death image is added.'),
(138,175):('Same.','Retain Samwell\'s terse agreement inside both the Emilio-present and Samwell-present predicates. Do not flatten the nested optional replies into an unconditional crew chorus.'),
(138,185):("Ha ha, we're stocked today! To make up for last time, you'll get my best meal!",'Retain the cheerful assurance about today\'s supplies, apology callback and promise to cook with special effort. The future tense promises food rather than claiming it has already been eaten.'),
(138,188):('I... I may have made things harder for you...','Restore Lil\'s personal, hesitant concern before she explains the lost customer. Do not substitute a collective we or state the causal harm with certainty.'),
(138,191):('How so?','Retain the barkeep\'s natural request for an explanation, giving Lil\'s next speech room to develop her concern.'),
(138,195):("Nagarpur was a good customer, wasn't he? He spent so much here...",'Correct the name and remove the unsupported best-customer superlative. Preserve Lil\'s tentative assessment based on his spending and her concern for the barkeep.'),
(138,207):('Well, you could say that...','Restore Fernando\'s qualified agreement rather than making his concession unequivocal. Keep it within his separate optional branch.'),
(138,214):("He did pay well. But back then... I think I'd lost my dignity.",'Restore the barkeep\'s reflective uncertainty and moral dignity rather than an ambiguous loss of personal pride. This prepares the confession about fawning over money.'),
(138,217):("I fawned over him for his money, did whatever he wanted... I'm ashamed of myself.",'Restore the source self-abasement for Nagarpur\'s money and the barkeep\'s shame in idiomatic first-person speech. Do not invent criminal acts or change the target of the self-criticism.'),
(138,221):('Oh, sir...','Retain Lil\'s sympathetic, hesitant address after the confession. Ordinary Sir supplies no kinship or new plot claim.'),
(138,225):("You said, 'There are things money can't buy,' remember? That opened my eyes.",'Restore the direct callback to Lil\'s earlier saying using the reviewed B137 wording. Preserve that her words changed the barkeep\'s outlook, rather than replacing the remembered speech with an unconnected maxim.'),
(138,236):('Yes! A fine line!','Retain Manuel\'s dignified, enthusiastic approval of the saying. Fine line is a natural judgment of the quoted words and adds no new poetry-note action.'),
(138,243):('From now on, I want to live with dignity, like you.','Replace the stiff self-address this old man with a natural first-person resolution. Dignity connects to the preceding confession; no new rank, status or employment is asserted.'),
(138,246):("You're making me blush! Let's both do our best!",'Retain Lil\'s modest embarrassment and warm mutual encouragement. The source explicitly supports blushing/feeling embarrassed; this adds no romance.'),
(138,249):('Heh, thank you. Say, do you know what this is?','Retain the gentle thanks and natural change of subject after the emotional resolution. The next object remains unidentified.'),
(138,253):('?','Retain the second meaningful wordless question before the display. It is distinct from the earlier alternative reaction and needs its own exact native glyph check.'),
(138,257):('A customer left it to cover a tab. No idea what it is...','Retain the natural colloquial account and uncertainty. The donor stays an unnamed customer; the tab supplies the source drinking-bill context.'),
(138,261):('A leaf? What kind?','Retain Lil\'s uncertain identification as a leaf and natural follow-up question. It supplies no species or confirmed item identity; do not force Evergreen Lotus Leaf into her still-uninformed speech.'),
(138,265):('You take it, miss. No use to me.','Retain the barkeep\'s casual free offer and reason. Miss is familiar ordinary address; the fragments are natural spoken English and add no payment or relationship.'),
(138,268):('Thank you!','Retain Lil\'s straightforward enthusiastic gratitude as the final response to the offer.'),
}
